    "reservedKeyNote": "The TC* family this layer owns, disjoint from the feature layers' PACK-<NAME>-* prefix (base.contract.json idRules.reservedFixtureKeys names the same TC* family). TCGRP-* and tc_* are the browsable storefront catalogue; TCSHOP-PIM and TCDM-* are the PIM tree 5.0.0 adds. Reserved int ids, all at or above the base contract's intIdentityFloor 100000 and written verbatim with IDENTITY_INSERT by the serializer: AccessUser 100100-100103, EcomDetailsGroup 100110 (Images) and 100111 (Manuals), EcomFieldDisplayGroups 100120 (tc_specs), EcomProductField 100130-100135 (the six TCFIELD-* variant-editing settings rows, 4.1.1), EcomStockUnit 100201-100261. 5.0.0 adds: EcomShops 100130, EcomShopLanguageRelation 100131, EcomGroups 100140-100144, EcomShopGroupRelation 100145-100149, EcomProductCategoryField 100150-100177, EcomCompletionRules 100160-100163, DynamicStructures 100170, DynamicStructureLevels 100171-100172, EcomGroupRelations 100178-100181, EcomGroupProductRelation 100200-100260, EcomProductCategoryFieldTranslation 100300-100327. The ranges are per TABLE, so EcomProductField 100130-100135 and EcomShops 100130 do not collide; base.contract.json reserves 100135 for its own EcomProductCategoryTranslation row on the same principle.",
