    "expectedRowsNote": "Rows arrive by merge deserialize of merge/_sql/<Table>/*.yml (35 tables); every count equals the per-table row-file count in merge/merge-manifest.json (2,024 rows), which 5.0.0 regenerates from disk in both directions. 5.0.1 replaces the 30 bare-option EcomVariantOptionsProductRelation rows with the 36 full combinations the six two-group masters need (Foundry #1255, #1269), so that table goes 30 -> 36. 5.0.0 adds 140 rows in eleven tables for the PIM structure: EcomShops 1 (TCSHOP-PIM, ShopType 4), EcomShopLanguageRelation 1, EcomGroups +5 (16 -> 21: one GroupType 1 folder and four GroupType 2 data models), EcomGroupRelations +4, EcomShopGroupRelation +5, EcomGroupProductRelation +61 (every master to the data model of its band, IsPrimary false), EcomProductCategoryField +28 and EcomProductCategoryFieldTranslation +28 (the reference_category mirrors), EcomCompletionRules 4, DynamicStructures 1, DynamicStructureLevels 2. EcomProducts is UNCHANGED at 97 - the PIM tree adds relations, never products. Two figures here are corrections rather than changes: EcomShopGroupRelation read 4 while sixteen rows sat on disk (the twelve 4.1.3 added and never declared), and EcomPrices read 233 while 4.1.2 left 221 on disk. The three loose sql[] scripts write no catalogue row: demo-clock.sql creates its own _demoClock* tables and the scheduled task, email-stats.sql writes only telemetry rows, number-counters.sql only raises EcomNumbers counters. Advisory: the gate derives its own counts from the composition. ONE of the 35 tables is a HEAP: DynamicStructures has no primary key on DW 10.28, so the engine writes it with DELETE FROM [table] plus insert-all under Merge as well as Replace, and delivering the layer's single workspace row removes every Dynamic Workspace the host already had (measured, gate run 20260919-153644). The other 34 tables all carry a primary key and their merge deletes nothing. See the DynamicStructures predicate _why in config/sample-data-2.4.json and README 'The one hazard this workspace row carries'."
